{
  "kanda": "ayodhya",
  "sarga": 49,
  "title": "Rama crossed three rivers",
  "sourceUrl": "https://www.valmikiramayan.net/utf8/ayodhya/sarga49/ayodhyasans49.htm",
  "romanUrl": "https://www.valmikiramayan.net/utf8/ayodhya/sarga49/ayodhyaitrans49.htm",
  "translator": "K. M. K. Murthy",
  "introduction": [
    "Having traveled for a pretty long distance, Rama crossed Vedasruti, Gomati and Syandika rivers. He presses forward in the chariot talking with Sumantra."
  ],
  "closing": [
    "इति वाल्मीकि रामायणे आदि काव्ये अयोध्य काण्डे एकोनपञ्चाशः सर्गः",
    "Thus completes 49th chapter in the AyodhyaKanda of the glorious Ramayana of Valmiki, the work of a sage and the oldest epic."
  ],
  "verses": [
